      "text": "A region should be able to hold a binding referendum on its own independence.",
      "value": 2,
      "rationale": "Sardist parties pushed an independence referendum bill, which failed by one vote in 2012, and treat self-determination by popular vote as a core demand.",
      "sources": [
        "s1"
      ],
      "addedAs": "right-to-secede"
    },
    {
      "text": "Special autonomy status for a region should be strengthened, not left as granted by the central state.",
      "value": 2,
      "rationale": "Nationalists have long argued that the postwar autonomy statute was too limited and demand more powers.",
      "sources": [
        "s1",
        "s4"
      ],
      "addedAs": "regional-powers-revocable"
    },
    {
      "text": "Military bases and training ranges should not be concentrated in one region against its wishes.",
      "value": 2,
      "rationale": "Sardists oppose the environmental damage of military activity, noting that about 60% of Italy's military bases are on the island.",
      "sources": [
